# Python UTF-8 Encoding

The markdown files in this repo contain Unicode characters (e.g. `→`, em-dashes, smart quotes). Python on Windows defaults to `cp1252`, which cannot encode them and will crash with `UnicodeEncodeError`.

## Rule

Always set `PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8` and use the **repo venv** — never bare `python` (Windows Store stub). Prefer `.\tools.ps1` or `.venv\Scripts\python.exe`. See `python-tools-env.mdc`.

```powershell
# ❌ BAD — Store stub and/or cp1252
python -m tools manifest context_tools.cdd.cdd:Cdd

# ✅ GOOD
.\tools.ps1 manifest context_tools.cdd.cdd:Cdd
# or:
$env:PYTHONIOENCODING="utf-8"; .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m tools manifest context_tools.cdd.cdd:Cdd
```

This applies to every `python -m tools` invocation in every response, with no exceptions.
